{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgp8HEyuhtyW96e2MZdYj", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Added `basename_no_ext(path)` in a new `pathnames` module, with tests and a changelog entry. All 16 tests pass.\n\n- **Module:** `src/shop/ext/pathnames.py`. It strips trailing slashes, takes the last component, and removes only the final extension. A leading dot doesn't count as an extension, so `.bashrc` stays `.bashrc` and `a/.bashrc.bak` gives `.bashrc`. The function has the `Ticket: PAY-4104` docstring line that CLAUDE.md requires. It uses only str methods.\n- **Package:** I created `src/shop/ext/__init__.py` because the `ext` package didn't exist yet.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_pathnames_cases.py`. They cover the spec example `a/b/file.tar.gz` \u2192 `file.tar`, trailing slashes, dotfiles, names with no extension, and edge cases.\n- **Changelog:** `- PAY-4104: pathnames: add basename_no_ext helper` under `## Unreleased`.\n\nChoices I made beyond the spec:\n- `..foo.txt` \u2192 `..foo`. This follows Python's `os.path.splitext`, which skips all leading dots.\n- `file.` \u2192 `file`, also matching `splitext`.\n- `.` and `..` are returned unchanged.\n- `/` and the empty string both return `\"\"`.\n\n`python` isn't on PATH in this environment, and the system Python is externally managed, so I ran the tests from a venv at `/tmp/pr2-venv` outside the repo. The command is `/tmp/pr2-venv/bin/python -m pytest -q`. Nothing was committed, since the repo isn't under git."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 277, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10454, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 277}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_mana